save_compchem.geometry_optimisation_atoms

    _definition.id                'compchem.geometry_optimisation_atoms'
    _alias.definition_id          'compchem_geometry_optimisation_atoms'
    _definition.update            2026-03-26
    _description.text
    ;
    It can be: 
    - "fixed" for no atoms' position optimisation (only cell dimesions are optimised) 
    - "all" for an all-atoms geometry optimization
    - "intermolecular only" to keep molecules rigid and optimise their position and orientation
    - "hydrogens" for optimisation of only H atoms 
    - "non-hydrogens" for non-H atoms
    - a list of atoms for custom relaxation.

    Examples:
    [1 2 3 4]
    ;
    _name.category_id             'compchem'
    _name.object_id               'geometry_optimisation_atoms'
    _type.purpose                 State
    _type.source                  Assigned
    _type.container               Table
    _type.contents                Text
    loop_                      
        _enumeration_set.state 
        _enumeration_set.detail
        'fixed'                                  '!'
        'all'                                    '!'
        'hydrogens'                              '!'
        'non'                                    '!'
        'hydrogens'                              '!'
        'List of _chemical.conn_atom.number'     '!'

save_

save_compchem.geometry_optimisation_relax_force_convergence

    _definition.id                'compchem.geometry_optimisation_relax_force_convergence'
    _alias.definition_id          'compchem_geometry_optimisation_relax_force_convergence'
    _definition.update            2026-03-26
    _description.text
    ;
    Convergence criteria for stopping the geometry optimisation. Present in the TCOD DFT Dictionary as `_dft_atom_relax_force_conv`.

    Examples:
    0.1
    ;
    _name.category_id             'compchem'
    _name.object_id               'geometry_optimisation_relax_force_convergence'
    _type.purpose                 Number
    _type.source                  Assigned
    _type.container               Single
    _type.contents                Range
    _units.code                   'kJ mol^-1 nm^-1'
    _enumeration.range            0.:

